  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the Promenade du Cap-Martin, between Monaco and the Italian border, Madame BLEUE presents itself as an invitation to travel: a decor ranging from azure blue to the tropics and a menu of fresh produce with a touch of exoticism. It opens every day from 9am to midnight, with breakfast from 9am to 11am.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The Menton, Riviera &amp; Merveilles tourist office page (updated 04/06/2026, read on 25/11/2026) lists "Animals accepted" among the services and "Terrace" among the facilities. It counts 100 seats on the terrace and a single air-conditioned room. The restaurant's website does not mention dogs: the terrace or the room, the leash and the dog's size should be confirmed on 04 93 83 87 85.</p>
      <p>Kitchen from 12pm to 2pm and 7pm to 10pm, with a reduced menu from 2:30pm to 6:30pm according to the tourist office; closed all day Tuesday and Sunday evening. A la carte prices run from €25 to €38 according to the office; breakfast, served from 9am to 11am, costs €2.50 to €16. Payment by bank card, cash and meal vouchers.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: mention your dog when booking and ask for a table on the terrace.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Cap-Martin coastal trail, just below, makes for a lovely walk with your dog before or after the meal.</p>
